# An operator asks a fast verification to stop at its first red, and the run
# stops there, says what it did not run, and leaves no certificate a reader
# could take for a pass.
#
# The fixture builds a throwaway git checkout (ZE_REPO_ROOT) and seeds its
# stage-time history (tmp/ze-verify-stage-times.tsv) so every fast stage costs
# 100 seconds except `arch tier/check`, which costs a millisecond. The cost
# order therefore runs that stage first, and it is red because the checkout
# holds no internal/component. The fixture then runs the real
# `le verify current fast first-red` and asserts:
#
# - the progress line says where the run stopped and how many stages it did
#   not run;
# - the combined log records the stop after exactly one stage result, and the
#   failure index names a stage the run never reached;
# - the history gained one line, for the stage that ran, and none for the rest;
# - `le verify status check` answers STALE for the stopped run.
#
# Delete the first-red stop in RunMode (internal/le/verify/engine/run.go,
# `plan.FirstRed && stageReport.Code != 0`) and seq=1 fails: the run goes on
# to the next stage.

option=timeout:value=120s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture runner/verify-first-red-stops
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=cheap-red-stage-seeded
expect=stdout:contains=run-stopped-at-first-red
expect=stdout:contains=log-names-unreached-stages
expect=stdout:contains=history-holds-only-the-reached-stage
expect=stdout:contains=status-answers-stale
